#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Headless Claude agents that outlive the hub: agent spawn | status | send | stop
(also callable as agent-spawn / agent-status / agent-send / agent-stop).

Long work (a merge steward, a release rehearsal, anything > 1 h) runs as a detached `claude -p`
session instead of a hub sub-agent: it survives the hub's handoff, and any hub can talk to it.

  agent spawn --role R --cwd DIR --model MODEL [--effort LEVEL] --brief FILE
              [--worktree [BRANCH] [--base REF]] [--stage S] [--tag T] [--title "…"] [--reason "…"]
              [--permission-mode MODE] [--mcp inherit|none|FILE[,FILE]] [--ignore-hold]
  agent status [R] [--stage S] [--all]
  agent send [--stage S] [--resume-anyway] R "msg"   (the options may stand anywhere before `--`; everything after the role
                                                      is the message, a word starting with `-` included)
  agent stop R [--stage S]
  agent worktrees [--repo PATH] [--json] [--fetch] [--no-gh] [--prune [--dry-run] [--delete-branches] [--no-fetch] [--idle-for DUR]]

Files: <hub home>/<stage>/agents/<R>/ — log.jsonl (stream-json of every run), stderr.log, meta.json,
brief.md (copy of the brief), inbox.md (messages while the agent runs), prompt-<run>.txt (the prompt of each run, written once).
spawn: `claude -p` with a fixed --session-id, --output-format stream-json --verbose and a permission mode
(default bypassPermissions: nobody is there to approve a tool call; $AGENT_HUB_PERMISSION_MODE or
--permission-mode changes it), in its own session and process group (setsid): it survives the calling shell and
the calling session. The prompt (brief and footer, or a resume message) is the run's stdin, read from prompt-<run>.txt, for
both engines (`claude -p`, `codex exec -`): never argv, which `ps` shows to every `pkill -f`.
The hub home is the caller's, pinned in the agent's $AGENT_HUB_HOME, and granted with `--add-dir <hub home>` when it is not under the agent's cwd (spawn and every
resume): the agent writes its journal lines and report there without a prompt, also under the Bash sandbox.
The agent gets HUB_TAG=<tag>, HUB_STAGE and this
plugin's bin/ first on PATH and in $HUB_BIN (the brief footer names jlog as "$HUB_BIN/jlog", since a shell may put
an old same-named tool ahead; every resume rebuilds the variable, so it follows a plugin update); it is recorded in `roles` (kind headless, pid).
Model: an alias (opus, sonnet, haiku, fable) or a full id claude-…. An alias follows the CLI: a current Claude Code
resolves it to the latest model of that family; Claude Code 2.1.287 is the minimum supported version (an older one
resolves it to an older model), and spawn warns about it. `haiku` is Haiku 5.5 from Claude Code 2.1.296, Haiku 4.5
before it. The id the run reports in its init event is recorded (meta resolved_model) and shown by status, the journal line
and agent-top. $AGENT_HUB_MODEL_MAP pins aliases to ids ("sonnet=claude-sonnet-x-y,opus=…") — an opt-in, since a pin
goes stale with the next model release.
Effort: --effort, else the model's entry in $AGENT_HUB_EFFORT_DEFAULTS, else $AGENT_HUB_DEFAULT_EFFORT, else high;
the same for every model, haiku included (Haiku 5.5 has the setting; Haiku 4.5 takes the flag and ignores it). An
effort above the model's default, or a model of $AGENT_HUB_REASON_MODELS, needs
--reason "…" (warning, or refusal with AGENT_HUB_REASON_POLICY=refuse); the reason goes into the journal start line
and meta.json (bin/spawn_policy.py). The title registered for the agent is `<role> — <the brief's first heading,
without a leading "Brief:"> (<stage>)`, unless --title says otherwise.
Load hold: while `bin/watchdog` holds spawns for machine load (AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_HOLD_LOAD, off by default), spawn warns
or, with AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_HOLD=refuse, refuses (exit 1); --ignore-hold passes. `send` is never held (bin/spawn_hold.py).
Limit pace: spawn compares fresh remaining weekly room for this launch, suggesting an equivalent engine/model/effort
below 20% remaining and respecting AGENT_HUB_STAGE_ENGINES. No model is swapped silently. Below 3% remaining it
refuses (exit 1) only with fresh data on both engines; --reason passes and is journalled. Forecasts, including the
low-confidence first six hours, are context only. Stale/unknown data never grounds refusal. Each crossing journals
one `@hub LIMIT …` line. AGENT_HUB_LIMIT_PACE=warn|off (bin/limit_pace.py).
--dry-run runs every check and prints the advice, then stops before anything is started or written.
A stage closed by `hub close` refuses spawn (exit 2) until a takeover reopens it.
Background sub-agents: a `claude -p` run whose turn ended waits for its background sub-agents only up to the
CLI's ceiling (10 min, then they are killed); an agent's run waits until they finish
(CLAUDE_CODE_PRINT_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS=0, or $AGENT_HUB_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS milliseconds).
These settings (and CLAUDE_BIN, AGENT_INIT_TIMEOUT, AGENT_HUB_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS) may also come from config.json
of the agent's repository (<repo>/.agent-hub/) or of the hub home; a brief-footer.md there is appended to the
footer of every brief.
--worktree: the agent works in a git worktree of BRANCH (default agent/<R>): an existing worktree of that branch is
reused wherever it is, so a re-spawn continues the work; otherwise <repo>/.worktrees/<BRANCH> of the main repository,
with /.worktrees/ added to .git/info/exclude (never untracked noise). A BRANCH that does not exist is created from
origin's default branch (origin/HEAD, else origin/main, else origin/master) after a bounded `git fetch origin
<default>` — not from the commit --cwd has checked out, which may be a foreign feature branch; the fetch failing
falls back to the local ref with a note, and a repository with no origin starts from its local main/master, else HEAD.
--base REF starts the new branch from REF instead (--base HEAD: the checked-out commit of --cwd, the old behaviour).
An existing branch or worktree is used as it is (--base is ignored with a note). The "worktree … created" line names
the base. status and stop name the worktree. Two agents in one checkout overwrite each other's files: give each writer
its own worktree. `agent worktrees` lists every worktree of the repository (path, branch, who made it, in use or not,
dirty or not, on a remote or not, merged or not, age) and, with --prune, removes the finished ones.
status: alive or not, the model, age of the last log event, model turns (of the last run, with the total once the
agent was resumed), the context size (ctx, the last model call's input), the last assistant text line.
send: alive → appended to inbox.md, journaled as "@<tag> msg" and kept as unread; process gone →
the session is resumed detached with `claude --resume <id> -p` (the message on stdin) in the same cwd, the unread
messages replayed first (an agent that ended its turn before reading its inbox loses nothing;
agent status flags them). spawn and resume succeed only once the run writes its init event
(120 s, $AGENT_INIT_TIMEOUT); a CLI that rejects its flags is killed and reported, and no role is recorded.
A resume is refused while the agent's context is above $AGENT_HUB_RESUME_MAX_CTX (default 250k tokens): spawn a fresh
agent from a handoff file; --resume-anyway overrides.
stop: SIGTERM to the process group (SIGKILL after 10 s), role retired.
worktrees: the ledger of one repository's git worktrees (--repo PATH, default the repository of the working directory),
read-only unless --prune; --json for the same table as data. Who made a worktree: an agent run (meta.json of any known
hub home), a hub (`<repo>/.claude/worktrees/<stage>-hub-<n>`), a registered role, else "other" (Desktop, manual). In use:
a live agent, the stage's registered hub, or any process whose working directory is inside it ("unknown" for a worktree
none of these knows). Merged: the branch is an ancestor of the remote default branch, or its HEAD is inside a pull
request merged into it (`gh pr list --state merged --head BRANCH`; a squash merge leaves no ancestry). --prune removes a
worktree (`git worktree remove`, never --force) only when it is merged, clean, has nothing unpushed, no git operation
under way, is not locked, not your working directory, not in use — and, where use is "unknown", has not changed for
--idle-for (default 24h); then `git worktree prune`. Its branch goes with it when merged by ancestry (`git branch -d`);
a squash-merged branch stays unless --delete-branches. `git worktree prune --expire=<idle limit>` clears the entries
of directories that have been gone that long (a moved worktree looks the same, sooner). --dry-run prints what would go.
The remote refs are as last fetched: --fetch runs `git fetch origin` first for a listing, and --prune does it unless
--no-fetch. --no-gh skips the pull-request lookup. Files git ignores (build output, a local .env) go with the worktree.
CLI binary: $CLAUDE_BIN, else the newer of `claude` on PATH and the newest CLI bundled with Claude Desktop (macOS);
spawn prints which one it took.
spawn warns (one line on stderr, never a refusal) while the stage's register has no owner-approved plan: the plan is shown to
the owner first, `ask plan` is recorded only after the owner's yes.
Exit: 0 ok, 1 failure / unknown agent, 2 usage.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import fcntl
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import uuid
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import hubcore as hc  # noqa: E402
import engines  # noqa: E402
import spawn_hold  # noqa: E402
import spawn_policy  # noqa: E402
import limit_pace  # noqa: E402
import worktrees  # noqa: E402

import importlib.machinery  # noqa: E402
import importlib.util  # noqa: E402

# `roles` is a script without .py; load it as a module to reuse set_role/retire_role.
_loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("roles_cli", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "roles"))
_spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("roles_cli", _loader)
roles_cli = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
_loader.exec_module(roles_cli)

# `ask` is a script without .py too; loaded on demand for the plan check of spawn.
def plan_warning(stage: str) -> str | None:
    """One line when the stage's register (`ask`) holds no owner-approved plan (`ask plan`), else None. The implicit
    `default` stage is a minimal-mode stage without a plan; an unreadable register says nothing."""
    if stage == hc.DEFAULT_STAGE:
        return None
    try:
        loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("ask_register", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "ask"))
        mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader("ask_register", loader))
        sys.modules["ask_register"] = mod  # dataclasses look the module up while the class is built
        loader.exec_module(mod)
        if mod.has_plan(stage):
            return None
    except Exception:
        return None
    return (f"stage {stage} has no owner-approved plan on record: show the plan to the owner; record `ask plan` "
            f"only after the owner's yes (`ask plan --stage {stage} \"<the plan in one line>\"`); spawning anyway")


ALIASES = hc.MODEL_ALIASES
EFFORTS = hc.EFFORTS
DEFAULT_PERMISSION_MODE = "bypassPermissions"


model_map = hc.model_map


STRIP_ENV = ("CLAUDECODE", "CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT", "CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID", "CLAUDE_CODE_SSE_PORT",
             "CODEX_THREAD_ID", "AGENT_SESSION_ID", "AGENT_HUB_CODEX_MODEL", "AGENT_HUB_CODEX_EFFORT") + engines.CODEX_APP_ENV

FOOTER = """
---
You are "{role}" (journal tag `{tag}`), stage `{stage}`, a headless {engine} session with nobody on the
other end: questions asked in chat are read by no one. The brief above is your contract.
- Talk to the hub only through the journal: `{jlog} "…"` (your tag is already in $HUB_TAG; run it by this
  path, $HUB_BIN is the plugin's bin/: another `jlog` earlier on PATH writes to a journal the hub does not read). Write only on events: MERGED / STOP /
  DONE / BLOCKED / a question. One line = status word, path, one sentence. The full report goes to `{report}`.
  A status word means "I have stopped, look now"; progress and milestones go to the report, or into a line that starts
  with PROGRESS and contains no status word.
- A question to the hub: `{jlog} "@hub QUESTION …"`, then end your turn with the word BLOCKED and the report
  path. The answer arrives as a new message in this same session (the hub runs `agent send {role} "…"`,
  which resumes the session).
- Messages that arrive while you work: `{inbox}` — read it after every major step and before finishing.
- The end of your turn is the end of the process. Keep long commands attached and wait for their completion
  through the host's execution tools; do not end your turn while a command you need still runs.
- Stop only processes you started, by the pid or process group you recorded; never `pkill -f` or `killall` with free
  text: it matches other agents' command lines.
- Never print environment variables or secret files. A secret the task needs stays inside your worktree and is
  removed before DONE.
- Commit unfinished work before long runs: an interrupted turn loses whatever is uncommitted.
"""


def footer(stage: str, cwd: Path, **fields) -> str:
    """The standard footer plus the first brief-footer.md of the config layers (stage, the agent's repository,
    hub home), with {role} {tag} {stage} {report} {inbox} {jlog} filled in."""
    fields["stage"] = stage
    fields.setdefault("engine", "claude")
    fields["jlog"] = '"$HUB_BIN/jlog"'  # not the path itself: a resumed run follows the plugin's current version
    text = FOOTER.format(**fields)
    extra = hc.config_file("brief-footer.md", stage, cwd)
    if extra:
        add = extra.read_text(encoding="utf-8").strip("\n")
        for k, v in fields.items():
            add = add.replace("{" + k + "}", str(v))
        text += add + "\n"
    return text


def git(*argv, cwd: Path) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    return subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(cwd), *argv], capture_output=True, text=True, env=hc.git_env())


WORKTREES_DIR = ".worktrees"


def _worktrees(top: Path) -> dict:
    """{branch: path} of every worktree of the repository (the main checkout included)."""
    res = git("worktree", "list", "--porcelain", cwd=top)
    out, path = {}, None
    for line in res.stdout.splitlines():
        if line.startswith("worktree "):
            path = Path(line[len("worktree "):])
        elif line.startswith("branch refs/heads/") and path is not None:
            out[line[len("branch refs/heads/"):]] = path
    return out


def worktree_base(top: Path, base: str | None) -> tuple[str, str]:
    """(ref, description) a new branch starts from: `base` as given (--base), else origin's default branch after a
    bounded fetch (a failed fetch falls back to the local ref, with a note on stderr), else — no such remote branch —
    the local default branch, else HEAD. Not --cwd's checked-out commit: that is whatever branch the clone has."""
    if base:
        return base, base
    ref, branch = hc.default_ref(top)
    if ref:
        failed = hc.fetch_default(top, branch)
        if failed:
            print(f"note: fetch of origin {branch} failed ({failed}): branching from the local {ref}", file=sys.stderr)
        return ref, ref
    if branch:
        print(f"note: {top} has no origin/{branch}: branching from the local {branch}", file=sys.stderr)
        return branch, branch
    print(f"note: {top} has no default branch to branch from: branching from HEAD", file=sys.stderr)
    return "HEAD", "HEAD"


def make_worktree(repo: Path, role: str, branch: str | None, base: str | None = None) -> tuple[Path, str, str]:
    """(path, branch, how) of the agent's worktree: an existing worktree of the branch is reused wherever it is ("reused");
    otherwise <main repository>/.worktrees/<branch>, with .worktrees/ in .git/info/exclude so it never shows as
    untracked ("created from <ref> <sha>"). A new branch starts from origin's default branch, or from `base`. A branch
    checked out in the main checkout is refused: that is not isolation."""
    res = git("rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir", cwd=repo)
    if res.returncode != 0:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--worktree: {repo} is not inside a git repository")
    common = Path(res.stdout.strip())
    top = common.parent if common.name == ".git" else Path(git("rev-parse", "--show-toplevel", cwd=repo).stdout.strip())
    branch = branch or f"agent/{role}"
    if git("check-ref-format", "--branch", branch, cwd=top).returncode != 0:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--worktree: {branch!r} is not a valid branch name")
    existing = _worktrees(top).get(branch)
    if existing is not None and not existing.is_dir():
        # a worktree directory deleted without `git worktree remove`: drop the stale entry, then create it afresh
        git("worktree", "prune", cwd=top)
        existing = _worktrees(top).get(branch)
        if existing is not None and not existing.is_dir():  # prune keeps a locked entry
            raise hc.Failure(f"--worktree: {branch} is registered at {existing}, which is gone, and the entry is "
                             f"locked — `git worktree unlock {existing}` (then `git worktree prune`), or pick another "
                             "branch")
    if existing is not None:
        if existing.resolve() == top.resolve():
            raise hc.UsageError(f"--worktree: {branch} is checked out in the main checkout {top} — pick another branch")
        if base:
            print(f"note: --base {base} ignored: {branch} already has a worktree", file=sys.stderr)
        return existing, branch, "reused"
    exists = git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", f"refs/heads/{branch}", cwd=top).returncode == 0
    start = ""
    if exists:
        if base:
            print(f"note: --base {base} ignored: branch {branch} exists", file=sys.stderr)
    else:
        ref, _ = worktree_base(top, base)
        # Explicit refs, especially HEAD, belong to the caller's checkout.
        # Resolve before using the common main checkout to create the worktree.
        res = git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", f"{ref}^{{commit}}", cwd=repo if base else top)
        if res.returncode != 0:
            if ref == "HEAD":
                # An unborn caller HEAD can coexist with commits on other refs.
                # Diagnose before exclude/worktree/agent files are created.
                commits = git("rev-list", "--all", "--max-count=1", cwd=repo)
                if commits.returncode != 0:
                    raise hc.Failure(f"--worktree: cannot inspect commits in {repo}: "
                                     f"{commits.stderr.strip() or commits.stdout.strip()}")
                if commits.stdout.strip():
                    raise hc.Failure(f"--worktree: HEAD in {repo} has no commits yet — this checkout's HEAD is "
                                     "unborn; commits exist on other refs. Use --base <existing branch/commit> "
                                     "or make a first commit on this branch; a worktree needs a commit to start from")
                raise hc.Failure(f"--worktree: the repository {repo} has no commits yet — make a first commit "
                                 "(`git commit --allow-empty -m \"first commit\"`); a worktree needs a commit to start from")
            raise hc.UsageError(f"--base {ref}: not a commit in {repo if base else top}")
        start = f"created from {ref} {res.stdout.strip()[:7]}"
        ref = res.stdout.strip()
    path = top / WORKTREES_DIR / branch
    if path.exists():
        raise hc.Failure(f"--worktree: {path} exists and is not a worktree of {branch} — remove it or pick another branch")
    exclude = common / "info" / "exclude"
    try:
        lines = exclude.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines() if exclude.exists() else []
        if f"/{WORKTREES_DIR}/" not in lines:
            exclude.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            with open(exclude, "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
                fh.write(("" if not lines or lines[-1] == "" else "\n") + f"/{WORKTREES_DIR}/\n")
    except OSError as e:
        print(f"note: could not add /{WORKTREES_DIR}/ to {exclude}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
    argv = (["worktree", "add", str(path), branch] if exists
            else ["worktree", "add", "--no-track", "-b", branch, str(path), ref])
    res = git(*argv, cwd=repo)
    if res.returncode != 0:
        raise hc.Failure(f"git worktree add: {res.stderr.strip() or res.stdout.strip()}")
    return path, branch, start or "created"


def worktree_note(meta: dict) -> str:
    wt = meta.get("worktree")
    if not wt:
        return ""
    return f"worktree {wt['path']} ({wt['branch']}) — `git worktree remove {wt['path']}` once the branch is merged"


def agent_dir(stage: str, role: str) -> Path:
    if not role or "/" in role or role.startswith("."):
        raise hc.UsageError(f"bad role name {role!r}")
    return hc.root() / hc.check_stage(stage) / "agents" / role


class AgentLock:
    """Per-agent lock (`.agent.lock` in the agent's directory) around everything that reads meta.json, decides from it
    and writes it back or starts a process: `agent send` (queue or resume), and the observers' claim of a run's end.
    Blocking by default; with blocking=False a holder elsewhere leaves `held` False and the caller skips (an observer
    must not wait out a resume's init wait)."""

    def __init__(self, stage: str, role: str, blocking: bool = True):
        self.path, self.blocking, self.held, self.fh = agent_dir(stage, role) / ".agent.lock", blocking, False, None

    def __enter__(self):
        self.fh = open(self.path, "a")
        try:
            fcntl.flock(self.fh, fcntl.LOCK_EX | (0 if self.blocking else fcntl.LOCK_NB))
            self.held = True
        except BlockingIOError:
            self.fh.close()
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *exc):
        if self.held:
            fcntl.flock(self.fh, fcntl.LOCK_UN)
            self.fh.close()


def claude_bin(cwd=None) -> str:
    """The CLI to start (hubcore.find_claude: $CLAUDE_BIN, else the newer of `claude` on PATH and Claude Desktop's)."""
    cli = hc.find_claude(cwd)
    if not cli:
        raise hc.Failure("claude not found on PATH (set $CLAUDE_BIN)")
    return cli.path


def load_meta(stage: str, role: str) -> dict:
    try:
        return json.loads((agent_dir(stage, role) / "meta.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except FileNotFoundError:
        raise hc.Failure(f"no agent {role!r} in stage {stage} ({agent_dir(stage, role)})") from None


def save_meta(stage: str, role: str, meta: dict) -> None:
    hc.atomic_write(agent_dir(stage, role) / "meta.json", json.dumps(meta, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1) + "\n")


def alive(meta: dict) -> bool:
    pid = meta.get("pid")
    if not pid:
        return False
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        pass
    try:
        cmd = subprocess.run(["ps", "-ww", "-o", "command=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
    except OSError:
        return True
    return (meta.get("process_token") or meta["session_id"]) in cmd  # guards against a reused pid


def child_env(stage: str, tag: str) -> dict:
    env = {k: v for k, v in hc.child_env().items() if k not in STRIP_ENV}
    env.update({"HUB_TAG": tag, "HUB_STAGE": stage})
    return env


BG_WAIT_ENV = "CLAUDE_CODE_PRINT_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS"


def bg_wait_ceiling(cwd=None) -> str:
    """Milliseconds a run whose turn ended waits for its background sub-agents before the CLI kills them.
    The CLI's default (10 min) cuts a background sub-agent of a headless agent short; 0 waits until it finishes."""
    raw = str(hc.setting("AGENT_HUB_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS", cwd=cwd) or "0").strip()
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9]+", raw):
        raise hc.UsageError("AGENT_HUB_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS must be a whole number of milliseconds (0 = no ceiling)")
    return raw


MCP_CHOICES = ("inherit", "none")
MCP_DEFAULT = "none"  # an executor loads no MCP server unless its task needs one; "inherit" brings them back


def mcp_choice(given, cwd) -> object:
    """The MCP servers of a Claude agent's runs: "inherit" (the user's config, enabled plugins and claude.ai connectors,
    as an interactive session gets them), "none" (--strict-mcp-config: no server at all), or a list of absolute paths
    of MCP config files (--strict-mcp-config --mcp-config FILE…: only their servers). `given` is --mcp, else
    AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_MCP, else MCP_DEFAULT; files are comma-separated, a relative one of --mcp is relative to the working directory. A
    repository's config.json — its .agent-hub/config.json, or a hub home inside it (repository_home) — may choose
    inherit or none only: a file's servers are commands the CLI would start."""
    raw, origin = (given, "flag") if given else hc.setting_origin("AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_MCP", cwd=cwd)
    name = "--mcp" if origin == "flag" else "AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_MCP"
    raw = (raw or MCP_DEFAULT).strip()
    if raw in MCP_CHOICES:
        return raw
    cfg = None
    if origin == "project":
        cfg = hc.project_dir(cwd) / hc.CONFIG_DIRNAME / "config.json"
    elif origin == "home" and repository_home():
        cfg = hc.root() / "config.json"
    if cfg is not None:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_MCP in {cfg}, a repository's config.json: one of {MCP_CHOICES} — an MCP "
                            "config file goes in a hub home's config.json outside the repository, the environment or "
                            "--mcp")
    parts = [x.strip() for x in raw.split(",") if x.strip()]
    if not parts:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"{name}: one of {MCP_CHOICES}, or MCP config files")
    for part in parts:
        if not Path(part).expanduser().is_absolute() and origin != "flag":
            raise hc.UsageError(f"{name}: {part}: an MCP config file must be an absolute path (or ~/…)")
    return mcp_files([str(Path(x).expanduser().resolve()) for x in parts], name)


def repository_home() -> bool:
    """Whether the hub home is a repository's: AGENT_HUB_HOME "project" (<repo>/.agent-hub/local/), or a home under
    <git top>/.agent-hub/ — what a child that got the project home as $AGENT_HUB_HOME (hc.child_env) sees, its layer
    reading "env". A home the user named elsewhere is the user's, whatever its path contains."""
    home = hc.home()
    if home.layer == "project":
        return True
    path = home.path.resolve()
    top = hc._git_top(path)
    return top is not None and path.is_relative_to(top / hc.CONFIG_DIRNAME)


def mcp_files(files: list, name: str) -> list:
    """`files` when each is an MCP config the CLI takes (a JSON object with "mcpServers"); else a usage error. Run
    again before a resume: the CLI would fail on a file deleted or broken since the spawn."""
    for f in files:
        if Path(f).is_dir():
            raise hc.UsageError(f"{name}: {f}: is a directory, not an MCP config file")
        try:
            data = json.loads(Path(f).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except OSError:
            raise hc.UsageError(f"{name}: {f}: no such file (inherit, none, or MCP config files)") from None
        except ValueError as e:
            raise hc.UsageError(f"{name}: {f}: not valid JSON ({e})") from None
        if not (isinstance(data, dict) and isinstance(data.get("mcpServers"), dict)):
            raise hc.UsageError(f'{name}: {f}: not an MCP config (a JSON object with "mcpServers")')
    return files


def mcp_text(mcp) -> str:
    return mcp if isinstance(mcp, str) else "only " + ", ".join(mcp)


def mcp_args(meta: dict) -> list:
    """The CLI flags of an agent's MCP choice; an agent spawned before the choice existed inherits."""
    mcp = meta.get("mcp") or "inherit"
    if mcp == "inherit":
        return []
    return ["--strict-mcp-config"] + (["--mcp-config", *mcp] if isinstance(mcp, list) else [])


def init_timeout(cwd=None) -> int:
    """Seconds to wait for a run's init event (it comes after MCP servers connect): AGENT_INIT_TIMEOUT or 120."""
    try:
        return int(hc.setting("AGENT_INIT_TIMEOUT", cwd=cwd) or 120)
    except ValueError:
        raise hc.UsageError("AGENT_INIT_TIMEOUT must be a whole number of seconds") from None


def wait_for_init(proc, log: Path, offset: int, session_id: str, stderr: Path, timeout_s: int = 120,
                  engine: str = "claude") -> dict:
    """Block until the run writes its init event for this session and return it; kill the run and fail otherwise."""
    deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout_s
    while time.monotonic() < deadline:
        try:
            with open(log, "rb") as fh:
                fh.seek(offset)
                for raw in fh:
                    try:
                        ev = json.loads(raw)
                    except ValueError:
                        continue
                    if not isinstance(ev, dict):
                        continue
                    for event in engines.normalize_event(ev):
                        if event.get("type") == "system" and event.get("subtype") == "init":
                            sid = event.get("session_id")
                            if (sid == session_id if session_id else isinstance(sid, str) and re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,100}", sid)):
                                return event
        except FileNotFoundError:
            pass
        if proc.poll() is not None:
            break
        time.sleep(0.3)
    code = proc.poll()
    if code is None:
        try:
            os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            pass
    tail = stderr.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")[-600:].strip() if stderr.exists() else ""
    why = f"exited with code {code}" if code is not None else f"sent no init event in {timeout_s} s, killed"
    raise hc.Failure(f"{engine} {why}; stderr: {tail or '—'}")


def launch(meta: dict, prompt: str, resume: bool) -> int:
    d = Path(meta["dir"])
    engine = meta.get("engine", "claude")
    if engine == "codex":
        argv = engines.codex_argv(meta, prompt, resume)
    else:
        argv = claude_argv(meta, resume)
    log = d / "log.jsonl"
    offset = log.stat().st_size if log.exists() else 0
    note = 'marker=$1; python=$2; shift 2; "$@"; c=$?; "$python" "$0" exit-note "$AGENT_ROLE" --stage "$HUB_STAGE" --code "$c" >&2; exit $c'
    token = meta.get("process_token") or meta["session_id"]
    argv = ["/bin/sh", "-c", note, str(Path(__file__).resolve()), token, sys.executable] + argv
    env = child_env(meta["stage"], meta["tag"])
    env.update({"AGENT_ROLE": meta["role"], "AGENT_SESSION_ID": meta["session_id"], "AGENT_HUB_ENGINE": engine})
    if engine == "codex" and meta.get("sandbox") == "workspace-write" and not is_review_role(meta):
        engines.prepare_worktree_sandbox(meta, env)
    if engine == "claude":
        env[BG_WAIT_ENV] = bg_wait_ceiling(meta["cwd"])
        env.setdefault(hc.IDLE_COMPACT_ENV, hc.IDLE_COMPACT_NEVER)
    else:
        env.update({"PLUGIN_ROOT": str(hc.BIN.parent), "CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT": str(hc.BIN.parent),
                    "AGENT_HUB_CODEX_MODEL": meta.get("model") or "", "AGENT_HUB_CODEX_EFFORT": meta.get("effort") or ""})
    # The prompt is the run's stdin, never argv: `ps` shows every command line, so a hub's `pkill -f "<words of the
    # brief>"` would otherwise kill the agents whose briefs hold the words (N2-01).
    # One file per run, created exclusively and never rewritten: a run reads exactly the prompt it was started with.
    run_id = uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]
    stdin_file = d / f"prompt-{run_id}.txt"
    fd = os.open(stdin_file, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        fh.write(prompt)
    with open(log, "ab") as out, open(d / "stderr.log", "ab") as err, open(stdin_file, "rb") as inp:
        proc = subprocess.Popen(argv, cwd=meta["cwd"], stdin=inp, stdout=out, stderr=err,
                                env=env, start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
    # The run is on record from the moment it exists: an observer that finds the pid gone then sees this run's pid, not
    # the previous run's (a resumed agent would otherwise look dead until the init event).
    before = (meta.get("pid"), list(meta.get("runs") or []))
    meta["pid"] = proc.pid
    meta.setdefault("runs", []).append({"pid": proc.pid, "at": hc.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
                                        "kind": "resume" if resume else "spawn", "prompt": stdin_file.name})
    save_meta(meta["stage"], meta["role"], meta)
    try:
        init = wait_for_init(proc, log, offset, meta["session_id"], d / "stderr.log", init_timeout(meta["cwd"]), engine)
    except hc.Failure:
        meta["pid"], meta["runs"] = before[0], before[1]
        save_meta(meta["stage"], meta["role"], meta)
        raise
    meta["session_id"] = init["session_id"]
    model = init.get("model")
    if isinstance(model, str) and hc.MODEL_VALUE_RE.fullmatch(model):
        meta["resolved_model"] = model
    return proc.pid


def claude_argv(meta: dict, resume: bool) -> list:
    """The command line of a run; the prompt is not in it: `-p` without a prompt argument reads it from stdin."""
    # Session flags first: the id stays at the head of `ps` output.
    argv = [claude_bin(meta["cwd"])]
    argv += ["--resume", meta["session_id"]] if resume else ["--session-id", meta["session_id"]]
    argv += ["--model", meta["model"]]
    if meta.get("effort"):
        argv += ["--effort", meta["effort"]]
    argv += ["--output-format", "stream-json", "--verbose",
             "--permission-mode", meta.get("permission_mode") or DEFAULT_PERMISSION_MODE]
    argv += mcp_args(meta)  # before --add-dir: --mcp-config takes several values too
    argv += hc.add_dir_args(meta["cwd"])  # before -n / -p: --add-dir takes several values
    if not resume:
        argv += ["-n", meta["title"]]
    return argv + ["-p"]


def model_name(meta: dict) -> str:
    """The model of an agent: the id its run reported, else the one requested (`sonnet`, or a pinned id)."""
    return meta.get("resolved_model") or meta["model"] or "CLI default"


def model_text(meta: dict) -> str:
    """model_name, plus what was asked for when the CLI resolved it to something else (an alias)."""
    got = meta.get("resolved_model")
    return f"{got} (asked for {meta['model']})" if got and got != meta["model"] else model_name(meta)


def journal(stage: str, fallback_tag: str, text: str) -> str:
    """One journal line under the caller's tag (HUB_TAG, else the registry entry of the calling session), else
    `fallback_tag`."""
    return hc.journal_append(stage, hc.caller_tag(stage) or fallback_tag, text)


def pace_advice(stage: str, engine: str, model_names: list, effort: str, task_class, reason: str, dry: bool) -> str:
    """The limit-pace advice for a launch (bin/limit_pace.py), printed before anything starts; a refusal is raised.
    Returns a note for the journal start line when the launch goes ahead over the hard-stop case, else ""."""
    if limit_pace.mode() == "off":
        return ""
    adv = limit_pace.advise(engine, " ".join(model_names), effort, stage, limit_pace.read_all(), task_class, reason,
                            limit_pace.stage_lock(stage))
    if adv.lines:
        print("limit pace — before this launch:\n" + "\n".join("  " + ln for ln in adv.lines))
    if adv.pace is not None:
        crossed = limit_pace.note_crossing(stage, adv.pace, write=not dry)
        if crossed and dry:
            print(f"dry run: would journal [{limit_pace.TAG}] {crossed}")
    if adv.refuse:
        raise hc.Failure(adv.refuse)
    if adv.stop:
        why = "--reason" if reason else "AGENT_HUB_LIMIT_PACE=warn"
        return f"over the limit-pace stop ({limit_pace.short(adv.pace)}) by {why}"
    return ""


def cmd_spawn(a) -> int:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage or hc.default_stage())
    if (closed := hc.stage_closed(stage)) is not None:  # `hub close`: nothing watches it, nothing lists its agents
        raise hc.UsageError(f"stage {stage} is closed ({closed.get('at')}: {closed.get('why')}) — reopen it with "
                            f"`hub takeover --stage {stage} --session …` before starting agents there")
    cwd = Path(a.cwd).expanduser().resolve()
    brief = Path(a.brief).expanduser().resolve()
    if not cwd.is_dir():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--cwd {cwd}: no such directory")
    # Settings come from the agent's repository (its .agent-hub/config.json), not from the caller's.
    engine = engines.selected(a.engine, cwd)
    if engine == "claude" and not a.model:
        raise hc.UsageError("--model is required for Claude")
    given_model = a.model or (hc.setting("AGENT_HUB_CODEX_DEFAULT_MODEL", cwd=cwd) if engine == "codex" else None)
    mmap = model_map(cwd) if engine == "claude" else engines.model_map(cwd)
    problem = (hc.model_problem(given_model, cwd) if engine == "claude" else engines.model_problem(given_model, cwd)) if given_model else None
    if problem:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--model: {problem}")
    given, a.model = given_model, mmap.get(given_model, given_model)
    allowed_efforts = EFFORTS if engine == "claude" else engines.CODEX_EFFORTS
    model_names = [n for n in dict.fromkeys([given or "CLI default", a.model or "CLI default"])]
    default_effort = spawn_policy.default_effort(model_names, allowed_efforts, cwd)
    effort = a.effort or default_effort
    if effort not in allowed_efforts:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"effort {effort!r} ({engine}): one of {allowed_efforts}")
    reason = spawn_policy.clean_reason(a.reason)
    above_default = spawn_policy.check_reason(model_names, effort, default_effort, allowed_efforts, reason, cwd,
                                              model_unknown=engine == "codex" and not a.model)
    if above_default:
        hc.warn(above_default)
    # AGENT_HUB_EFFORT_RULES: the model x effort policy shared with the delegation hook (bin/subagent_rules.py)
    import subagent_rules  # noqa: E402
    denied = subagent_rules.check_spawn(given or "CLI default", a.model or "CLI default", effort, cwd)
    if denied:
        raise hc.UsageError(denied)
    if engine == "codex" and a.mcp and a.mcp != "inherit":
        # `codex exec -c` cannot switch off the servers of Codex plugins; AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_MCP is for Claude agents
        raise hc.UsageError("--mcp is only supported by the Claude engine")
    mcp = mcp_choice(a.mcp, cwd) if engine == "claude" else None  # before pace_advice, which may journal
    pace_note = pace_advice(stage, engine, model_names, effort, a.task_class, reason, a.dry_run)
    pmode = a.permission_mode or hc.setting("AGENT_HUB_PERMISSION_MODE", cwd=cwd) or DEFAULT_PERMISSION_MODE
    sandbox = None
    policy = None
    if engine == "codex":
        if a.sandbox_policy:
            policy = engines.sandbox_policy(a.sandbox_policy)
            sandbox = policy["type"]
            if a.sandbox and a.sandbox != sandbox:
                raise hc.UsageError("--sandbox and --sandbox-policy type disagree")
            if a.permission_mode and engines.permission_policy(a.permission_mode, cwd=cwd) != sandbox:
                raise hc.UsageError("--permission-mode and --sandbox-policy type disagree")
        else:
            sandbox = engines.permission_policy(a.permission_mode, a.sandbox, cwd)
        if sandbox == "workspace-write" and engines.is_review_role({"role": a.role, "tag": a.tag}):
            engines.workspace_write_roots({"role": a.role, "tag": a.tag, "cwd": str(cwd),
                                           "sandbox_policy": policy})
        engines.hook_args(cwd)
    elif a.sandbox or a.sandbox_policy:
        raise hc.UsageError("--sandbox and --sandbox-policy are only supported by the Codex engine")
    else:
        bg_wait_ceiling(cwd)  # a bad value fails before any directory or process exists
    if not brief.is_file():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--brief {brief}: no such file")
    if a.base and a.worktree is None:
        raise hc.UsageError("--base goes with --worktree: it names the commit the worktree's new branch starts from")
    if engine == "claude":
        cli = hc.find_claude(cwd)
        if cli is None:
            raise hc.Failure("claude not found on PATH, and no CLI is bundled with Claude Desktop (set $CLAUDE_BIN)")
        print(f"CLI {cli.describe()}")
        old_cli = hc.cli_warning(cli)
        if old_cli:
            hc.warn(old_cli)
    else:
        print(f"CLI {engines.codex_bin(cwd)} (codex)")
    no_plan = plan_warning(stage)
    if no_plan:
        hc.warn(no_plan)
    for w in hc.project_warnings(cwd):
        print(f"ATTENTION: {w}")
    own = hc.caller_tag(stage)
    if own and hc.tag_is(a.tag or a.role, own):
        # jwait drops the caller's own tag and its sub-tags: the agent's DONE would never wake the hub
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--tag {a.tag or a.role!r} is a sub-tag of your own tag {own!r}; jwait would never "
                            f"deliver its lines — use {own}-{a.role}")
    held = spawn_hold.gate(a.ignore_hold)  # the machine-load hold (bin/watchdog); a refusal is raised here
    if held:
        hc.warn(held)
    if a.dry_run:
        print(f"dry run: {a.role} would start on {engine} ({a.model or 'CLI default'}/{effort}) in {cwd}"
              f"{', MCP ' + mcp_text(mcp) if mcp and mcp != MCP_DEFAULT else ''}; nothing was started or written")
        return 0
    d = agent_dir(stage, a.role)
    if (d / "meta.json").exists():
        old = load_meta(stage, a.role)
        if alive(old):
            raise hc.Failure(f"agent {a.role} is already running (pid {old['pid']}); agent stop {a.role} or pick another name")
    wt = None
    if a.worktree is not None:
        path, branch, how = make_worktree(cwd, a.role, a.worktree or None, a.base)
        wt = {"path": str(path), "branch": branch}
        print(f"worktree {path} on {branch} ({how})")
        cwd = path
    if (d / "meta.json").exists():
        # a finished agent of the same name: keep its files, start a clean directory
        d.rename(d.with_name(f"{a.role}.{time.strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S')}"))
    d.mkdir(parents=True)
    hc.register_home()  # the stage now has an agents/ directory: its home is one agent-top lists (registry of homes)
    tag = a.tag or a.role
    shutil.copyfile(brief, d / "brief.md")
    (d / "inbox.md").write_text(f"# Inbox of agent {a.role}\n\n", encoding="utf-8")
    report = hc.work_dir(stage) / f"{tag.replace('/', '-')}-REPORT.md"
    meta = {"role": a.role, "tag": tag, "stage": stage, "session_id": str(uuid.uuid4()) if engine == "claude" else "", "model": a.model,
            "effort": effort, "permission_mode": pmode, "cwd": str(cwd), "dir": str(d), "brief": str(brief),
            "title": a.title or spawn_policy.brief_title(a.role, stage, brief.read_text(encoding="utf-8")),
            "report": str(report),
            "started_at": hc.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds"), "runs": []}
    meta["engine"] = engine
    if mcp:
        meta["mcp"] = mcp
    if reason:
        meta["reason"] = reason
    if engine == "codex":
        if sandbox == "read-only" and is_review_role(meta):
            hc.warn("Codex read-only reviewer cannot write its report or journal; "
                    "use workspace-write with --cwd in the hub home")
        meta.update({"sandbox": sandbox, "process_token": str(uuid.uuid4())})
        if sandbox == "workspace-write" and not is_review_role(meta):
            meta["sandbox_git_roots"] = engines.worktree_git_roots(cwd)
            if meta["sandbox_git_roots"]:
                hc.warn(engines.WORKTREE_SANDBOX_NOTE)
        if policy:
            meta["sandbox_policy"] = policy
    if wt:
        meta["worktree"] = wt
    prompt = brief.read_text(encoding="utf-8") + footer(stage, cwd, engine=engine, role=a.role, tag=tag, report=report,
                                                       inbox=d / "inbox.md")
    if meta.get("sandbox_git_roots"):
        prompt += "\n" + engines.WORKTREE_SANDBOX_NOTE + "\n"
    save_meta(stage, a.role, meta)
    try:
        pid = launch(meta, prompt, resume=False)
    except hc.Failure:
        d.rename(d.with_name(f"{a.role}.failed-{time.strftime('%Y%m%d-%H%M%S')}"))
        raise
    save_meta(stage, a.role, meta)  # launch recorded the pid and the run; this keeps the init event's session id
    roles_cli.set_role(stage, a.role, meta["session_id"], "headless", tag=tag, title=meta["title"],
                       note=f"agent-spawn {model_name(meta)}", pid=pid, cwd=str(cwd), log=str(d / "log.jsonl"))
    with hc.roles_lock(stage):
        data = hc.roles_load(stage)
        data["roles"][a.role]["engine"] = engine
        if meta.get("process_token"):
            data["roles"][a.role]["process_token"] = meta["process_token"]
        hc.roles_save(stage, data)
    got = meta.get("resolved_model")
    line = journal(stage, tag, f"started headless agent {a.role} ({model_name(meta)}{'/' + effort if effort else ''}"
                               f"{', asked for ' + a.model if got and a.model and got != a.model else ''}), "
                               f"session {meta['session_id']}, pid {pid}, brief {brief}"
                               + (f", worktree {wt['path']} ({wt['branch']})" if wt else "")
                               + (f", MCP {mcp_text(mcp)}" if mcp and mcp != MCP_DEFAULT else "")
                               + (f", reason: {reason}" if reason else "")
                               + (f", {pace_note}" if pace_note else ""))
    print(f"started {a.role}: pid {pid}, session {meta['session_id']}\nlog {d / 'log.jsonl'}\n{line}")
    return 0


def read_log(path: Path) -> dict:
    """What the log of every run of the agent says: model turns (all runs, and the last run's), the last assistant
    text, the last result, whether a run started after it, the context size (the last model call's input: input plus
    cache tokens of the last main-thread assistant message — what agent-top shows as ctx; 0 when the log has none)."""
    turns, run_turns, last_text, results, last_type, ctx = set(), set(), "", [], "", 0
    started_after_result = False
    try:
        fh = open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return {"turns": 0, "run_turns": 0, "last_text": "", "result": None, "events": 0, "running_after_result": False,
                "ctx": 0}
    n = 0
    with fh:
        for raw in fh:
            try:
                events = engines.normalize_event(json.loads(raw))
            except ValueError:
                continue
            for ev in events:
                n += 1
                t = ev.get("type")
                if ev.get("_engine") == "codex":
                    if t == "system" and ev.get("subtype") == "turn_start":
                        turns.add(n)
                        run_turns.add(n)
                        started_after_result = True
                        continue
                    if t == "system" and ev.get("subtype") == "init":
                        run_turns = set()
                    if t == "assistant":
                        for block in (ev.get("message") or {}).get("content") or []:
                            if block.get("type") == "text" and block.get("text", "").strip():
                                last_text = [ln for ln in block["text"].splitlines() if ln.strip()][-1].strip()
                        continue
                    if t == "result":
                        ev["result"] = last_text
                if t == "system" and ev.get("subtype") == "init":
                    started_after_result = True
                    run_turns = set()
                elif t == "assistant":
                    msg = ev.get("message") or {}
                    usage = msg.get("usage")
                    if isinstance(usage, dict) and not ev.get("parent_tool_use_id"):  # a sub-agent's call is not this context
                        ctx = sum(int(usage.get(k) or 0) for k in ("input_tokens", "cache_read_input_tokens",
                                                                   "cache_creation_input_tokens")) or ctx
                    turns.add(msg.get("id") or n)
                    run_turns.add(msg.get("id") or n)
                    for block in msg.get("content") or []:
                        if block.get("type") == "text" and block.get("text", "").strip():
                            last_text = [ln for ln in block["text"].splitlines() if ln.strip()][-1].strip()
                elif t == "result":
                    results.append(ev)
                    started_after_result = False
                last_type = t
    return {"turns": len(turns), "run_turns": len(run_turns), "last_text": last_text,
            "result": results[-1] if results else None, "events": n, "running_after_result": started_after_result,
            "last_type": last_type, "ctx": ctx}


def turns_text(info: dict) -> str:
    """"31" for an agent with one run, "31 (total 60)" once a resumed run's turns differ from the total."""
    if info["run_turns"] != info["turns"]:
        return f"{info['run_turns']} (total {info['turns']})"
    return str(info["turns"])


def pending_unread(meta: dict) -> list:
    """Unread messages the agent's log does not show as handled: after the message was queued the
    agent neither touched inbox.md in a tool call nor ended a run with DONE."""
    unread = meta.get("inbox_unread") or []
    if not unread:
        return []
    log = Path(meta["dir"]) / "log.jsonl"
    try:
        data = log.read_bytes()
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return unread
    pending = []
    for u in unread:
        handled = False
        for raw in data[u.get("log_offset", 0):].splitlines():
            try:
                ev = json.loads(raw)
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if ev.get("type") == "assistant":
                for block in (ev.get("message") or {}).get("content") or []:
                    if block.get("type") == "tool_use" and "inbox.md" in json.dumps(block.get("input"), ensure_ascii=False):
                        handled = True
            elif ev.get("type") == "result" and re.search(r"\bDONE\b", str(ev.get("result") or "")):
                handled = True
            elif ev.get("type") == "item.completed":
                item = ev.get("item") or {}
                handled = ((item.get("type") == "command_execution" and "inbox.md" in item.get("command", "")
                            and item.get("exit_code") == 0) or
                           (item.get("type") == "agent_message" and re.search(r"\bDONE\b", item.get("text", ""))))
            if handled:
                break
        if not handled:
            pending.append(u)
    return pending


OBSERVE_WINDOW_S = 24 * 3600  # a run that died longer ago than this is history, not news


def process_gone(meta: dict) -> bool:
    """Whether the recorded run's process is certainly gone: no such pid, or a pid that now runs another command line.
    Unlike alive(), a `ps` that shows nothing (a sandbox hiding other processes) is not "gone": the observers below
    write to the journal once and for all, so they need a certain answer."""
    pid = meta.get("pid")
    if not isinstance(pid, int) or not pid:
        return False
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return True
    except PermissionError:
        pass
    try:
        cmd = subprocess.run(["ps", "-ww", "-o", "command=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
    except OSError:
        return False
    return bool(cmd.strip()) and (meta.get("process_token") or meta["session_id"]) not in cmd


def exit_marker(stage: str, meta: dict) -> Path:
    run = (meta.get("runs") or [{}])[-1]
    key = re.sub(r"[^\w.-]+", "_", f"{meta['role']}.{meta.get('pid')}.{run.get('at', '')}")
    return hc.state_dir() / "agent-exits" / stage / key


def claim_exit(stage: str, meta: dict) -> bool:
    """True for the first caller to claim the end of this agent's latest run (atomic: O_CREAT|O_EXCL on a marker under
    the state dir, never in the agent's own directory), False for every later one. The claim decides who writes the EXIT
    line, so it is written once however many observers (agent status, jwait, the exit-note wrapper) see the end."""
    path = exit_marker(stage, meta)
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    try:
        os.close(os.open(path, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o644))
    except FileExistsError:
        return False
    return True


BUSY = object()  # observe_death: a start or resume holds the agent's lock; try again later


def observe_death(stage: str, meta: dict, mtime) -> "str | object | None":
    """An agent whose process is gone without a result of its latest run (kill -9, a crash of the whole group: the
    exit-note wrapper died with it) is journaled once, by whoever notices first: `EXIT <role>: killed (no result)`,
    under the agent's tag, the line the hub's default jwait wakes on. Returns the line, None (nothing to report, or
    another observer wrote it, or nothing can be written here) or BUSY. Only for a recent death (`mtime` of the log); the caller checks the role is
    registered (agent stop retires it).

    The decision is made under the agent's lock, from what is on disk after the process is confirmed gone: the meta
    (a resume that started meanwhile changed the pid) and the log (a run that wrote its result and exited between the
    caller's read and now is not killed). A start or resume holds the lock for its whole init wait: no waiting here."""
    if mtime is None or hc.now().timestamp() - mtime.timestamp() > OBSERVE_WINDOW_S:
        return None
    try:
        with AgentLock(stage, meta["role"], blocking=False) as lock:
            if not lock.held:
                return BUSY
            try:
                fresh = load_meta(stage, meta["role"])
            except hc.Failure:
                return None
            if not process_gone(fresh):
                return None
            info = read_log(Path(fresh["dir"]) / "log.jsonl")
            if info["result"] and not info["running_after_result"]:
                return None
            if not claim_exit(stage, fresh):
                return None
            last = (info["last_text"] or "").strip().splitlines()
            try:
                return hc.journal_append(stage, fresh["tag"], f"EXIT {fresh['role']}: killed (no result); turns "
                                         f"{turns_text(info)}{'; last: ' + last[-1][:160] if last else ''} — agent status "
                                         f"{fresh['role']}")
            except OSError:
                exit_marker(stage, fresh).unlink(missing_ok=True)  # not written: the next observer may try
                raise
    except OSError:
        # A read-only sandbox (an agent running `agent status`): no lock file, marker or journal line can be written. The
        # observation is skipped; whatever the caller prints (a status line) is unaffected.
        return None


def _gone_agents(stage: str, memo: dict) -> list:
    """[(role, meta, log stat)] of the stage's registered agents whose process is gone and whose (pid, log size) the memo has
    not looked at yet: the scan that observe_dead and dead_candidates share."""
    base = hc.root() / stage / "agents"
    if not base.is_dir():
        return []
    registered = hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"]
    out = []
    for mp in sorted(base.glob("*/meta.json")):
        role = mp.parent.name
        if role not in registered:
            continue
        try:
            meta = json.loads(mp.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
            log = Path(meta["dir"]) / "log.jsonl"
            st = log.stat()
        except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError):
            continue
        if not isinstance(meta, dict) or not process_gone(meta) or memo.get(role) == (meta.get("pid"), st.st_size):
            continue
        out.append((role, meta, st))
    return out


def observe_dead(stage: str, memo: dict | None = None) -> list:
    """observe_death for every registered headless agent of the stage (jwait's poll). `memo` ({role: (pid, log
    size)}) keeps a run that was looked at from being read again until its pid or log changes."""
    memo = {} if memo is None else memo
    lines = []
    for role, meta, st in _gone_agents(stage, memo):
        line = observe_death(stage, meta, hc.dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(st.st_mtime, hc.TZ))
        if line is BUSY:
            continue  # looked at again on the next poll
        memo[role] = (meta.get("pid"), st.st_size)
        if line:
            lines.append(line)
    return lines


def dead_candidates(stage: str) -> list:
    """[(meta, log mtime)] of the agents observe_dead would journal as `EXIT … killed (no result)` right now, and
    nothing else: the same process, recency and result checks, but no lock, no claim and no write (`watchdog run
    --dry-run` lists them)."""
    out = []
    for _, meta, st in _gone_agents(stage, {}):
        mtime = hc.dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(st.st_mtime, hc.TZ)
        if hc.now().timestamp() - mtime.timestamp() > OBSERVE_WINDOW_S:
            continue
        info = read_log(Path(meta["dir"]) / "log.jsonl")
        if (info["result"] and not info["running_after_result"]) or exit_marker(stage, meta).exists():
            continue
        out.append((meta, mtime))
    return out


def status_line(stage: str, role: str) -> str:
    meta = load_meta(stage, role)
    log = Path(meta["dir"]) / "log.jsonl"
    info = read_log(log)
    try:
        mtime = hc.dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(log.stat().st_mtime, hc.TZ)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        mtime = None
    live = alive(meta)
    registry = hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"].get(role)
    if live:
        state = f"ALIVE (pid {meta['pid']})"
    elif info["result"] and not info["running_after_result"]:
        r = info["result"]
        cost = f", ${r['total_cost_usd']:.2f}" if isinstance(r.get("total_cost_usd"), (int, float)) else ""
        state = f"finished ({r.get('subtype')}{', error' if r.get('is_error') else ''}{cost})"
    else:
        state = "no process, no result (died or killed)"
    if registry is None:
        state += ", role retired"
    elif not live:
        observe_death(stage, meta, mtime)  # journals EXIT once when the process is gone without a result
    unread = pending_unread(meta) if not live else []
    if unread:
        state += (f"; unread inbox messages {len(unread)} since {unread[0]['at'][11:16]} — "
                  f"agent send {role} [text] resumes with them")
    text = info["last_text"][:220] + ("…" if len(info["last_text"]) > 220 else "")
    wt = meta.get("worktree")
    engine = meta.get("engine", "claude")
    return (f"{role} [{meta['tag']}] {engine}/{model_text(meta)}: {state}; last event {hc.age(mtime)} ago; "
            f"turns {turns_text(info)}; " + (f"ctx {spawn_policy.fmt_tokens(info['ctx'])}; " if info["ctx"] else "")
            + f"last: {text or '—'}" + (f"; worktree {wt['path']} ({wt['branch']})" if wt else ""))


def cmd_status(a) -> int:
    print(hc.plugin_runtime_line())
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage or hc.default_stage())
    if a.role:
        print(status_line(stage, a.role))
        return 0
    base = hc.root() / stage / "agents"
    names = sorted(p.parent.name for p in base.glob("*/meta.json")) if base.is_dir() else []
    live_roles = hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"]
    names = [n for n in names if n in live_roles] if not a.all else names
    if not names:
        print("no headless agents" + ("" if a.all else " (--all includes retired ones)")
              + ("" if base.is_dir() else hc.elsewhere_hint(stage)))
        return 0
    for n in names:
        print(status_line(stage, n))
    return 0


def cmd_worktrees(a) -> int:
    return worktrees.run(a, alive)


def cmd_send(a) -> int:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage or hc.default_stage())
    msg = hc.one_line(" ".join(a.text))
    load_meta(stage, a.role)  # an unknown agent fails before a lock file is made
    # Everything from reading meta.json to writing it back — the liveness decision, the queueing, the resume with its init
    # wait — is one critical section: two sends never both resume, a message queued while a resume starts is not
    # overwritten by the resume's older copy of the meta, and the resume's prompt file is its own.
    with AgentLock(stage, a.role):
        return _send_locked(stage, a, msg)


def legacy_effort(meta: dict) -> None:
    """A Claude agent spawned while Haiku took no effort has `effort: null` on record, and its resume would leave the effort
    to the CLI's own setting. Give it the effort a spawn would (AGENT_HUB_EFFORT_DEFAULTS, AGENT_HUB_DEFAULT_EFFORT, high),
    refuse what AGENT_HUB_EFFORT_RULES refuses, and put it in `meta` (launch saves it)."""
    if meta.get("effort"):
        return
    import subagent_rules  # noqa: E402
    cwd, model, resolved = Path(meta["cwd"]), meta["model"], meta.get("resolved_model") or meta["model"]
    effort = spawn_policy.default_effort(list(dict.fromkeys([model, resolved])), EFFORTS, cwd)
    denied = subagent_rules.check_spawn(model, resolved, effort, cwd)
    if denied:
        raise hc.UsageError(denied)
    meta["effort"] = effort


def _send_locked(stage: str, a, msg: str) -> int:
    meta = load_meta(stage, a.role)
    if a.role not in hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"]:
        raise hc.Failure(f"agent {a.role} was stopped (role retired); start a new one with agent spawn")
    live = alive(meta)  # one reading: the checks and the branch below must agree on it
    if not live:
        if meta.get("engine", "claude") == "claude":
            bg_wait_ceiling(meta["cwd"])  # the resume would refuse a bad setting: refuse before the message is queued
            legacy_effort(meta)  # likewise a rule that refuses the effort it would get
            if isinstance(meta.get("mcp"), list):  # likewise an MCP config file deleted or broken since the spawn
                mcp_files(meta["mcp"], f"agent {a.role}'s MCP config")
        if not a.resume_anyway:
            limit, ctx = spawn_policy.resume_max_ctx(meta["cwd"]), read_log(Path(meta["dir"]) / "log.jsonl")["ctx"]
            if limit and ctx > limit:  # refused before the message is queued
                raise hc.Failure(spawn_policy.resume_refusal(a.role, ctx, limit))
    t = hc.now()
    if msg:
        with open(Path(meta["dir"]) / "inbox.md", "a", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
            fh.write(f"- {t:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M} {msg}\n")
    if live:
        if not msg:
            raise hc.UsageError("the agent is alive — a message text is required")
        log = Path(meta["dir"]) / "log.jsonl"
        meta.setdefault("inbox_unread", []).append({"at": t.isoformat(timespec="seconds"), "msg": msg,
                                                    "log_offset": log.stat().st_size if log.exists() else 0})
        save_meta(stage, a.role, meta)
        line = journal(stage, "cli", f"@{meta['tag']} {msg}")
        print(f"agent alive (pid {meta['pid']}): queued in its inbox, read after its current step; if it ends its turn "
              f"unread, agent status shows it and the next agent send replays it\n{line}")
        return 0
    queued = list(meta.get("inbox_unread") or [])
    unread = pending_unread(meta)
    if not msg and not unread:
        raise hc.UsageError("empty message and no unread inbox messages")
    parts = []
    if unread:
        parts.append("Hub messages that arrived while you were working — your log shows you did not read them:\n"
                     + "\n".join(f"- {u['at'][11:16]} {u['msg']}" for u in unread))
    if msg:
        parts.append(msg)
    pid = launch(meta, "\n\n".join(parts) + "\n\n(A message from the hub. The rules for talking to the hub are at the end of "
                 "the brief above: journal, report, inbox.)",
                 resume=True)
    # only what this resume looked at leaves the queue (replayed, or already handled by the log)
    meta["inbox_unread"] = [u for u in meta.get("inbox_unread") or [] if u not in queued]
    save_meta(stage, a.role, meta)
    with hc.roles_lock(stage):
        data = hc.roles_load(stage)
        data["roles"][a.role]["pid"] = pid
        hc.roles_save(stage, data)
    line = journal(stage, "cli", f"@{meta['tag']} (session resumed, pid {pid}"
                                 + (f", unread replayed: {len(unread)}" if unread else "") + f") {msg}".rstrip())
    print(f"no process was running — session {meta['session_id']} resumed: pid {pid}\n{line}")
    return 0


def cmd_stop(a) -> int:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage or hc.default_stage())
    meta = load_meta(stage, a.role)
    how = "no process was running"
    if alive(meta):
        pgid = meta["pid"]
        try:
            claim_exit(stage, meta)  # a stop is a known end: no observer reports it as "killed"
        except OSError:
            pass
        try:
            os.killpg(pgid, signal.SIGTERM)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            pass
        for _ in range(20):
            if not alive(meta):
                break
            time.sleep(0.5)
        if alive(meta):
            try:
                os.killpg(pgid, signal.SIGKILL)
            except ProcessLookupError:
                pass
            time.sleep(0.5)
            how = "SIGKILL"
        else:
            how = "SIGTERM"
        if alive(meta):
            raise hc.Failure(f"pid {pgid} is alive after SIGKILL")
    if a.role in hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"]:
        roles_cli.retire_role(stage, a.role, "agent-stop")
    print(f"{a.role}: stopped ({how}), role retired")
    if worktree_note(meta):
        print(worktree_note(meta))
    return 0




def status_seen(stage: str, tag: str, since: hc.dt.datetime) -> bool:
    """Did the agent journal a status word (its own tag) since `since`? The words are the hub's wake words
    (hubcore.status_pattern: MERGED, STOP, DONE, BLOCKED, QUESTION, … plus $AGENT_HUB_JWAIT_MATCH)."""
    status_re = re.compile(hc.status_pattern(exit_word=False))
    day = since.date()
    while day <= hc.now().date():
        path = hc.journal_path(stage, day)
        if path.exists():
            for line in path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
                m = hc.JOURNAL_LINE_RE.match(line)
                if not m or not hc.tag_is(m.group(2), tag) or not status_re.search(m.group(3)):
                    continue
                hh, mm = map(int, m.group(1).split(":"))
                if hc.dt.datetime.combine(day, hc.dt.time(hh, mm), tzinfo=hc.TZ) >= since.replace(second=0, microsecond=0):
                    return True
        day += hc.dt.timedelta(days=1)
    return False


def is_review_role(meta: dict) -> bool:
    """A review role by its name or tag: `review-pr34`, `desktop-review`, `reviewer2` (the plugin's own reviewers are
    `review-<name>`), not `preview` or `reviewfix`. Legacy read-only reviewers cannot journal their verdict."""
    return engines.is_review_role(meta)


def cmd_exit_note(a) -> int:
    """Called by the launch shell after claude exits (either engine). A run that ended cleanly (code 0, a successful
    result) with a status word of its own in the journal needs no line. One that ended cleanly without one is journaled
    as the neutral `ENDED <role>` (`REVIEWED <role>` for a review role): the agent stopped and the hub wakes on it, but
    nothing looks wrong. EXIT stays for an abnormal end (a code, an error result, no result)."""
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage or hc.default_stage())
    meta = load_meta(stage, a.role)
    info = read_log(Path(meta["dir"]) / "log.jsonl")
    # a result of an earlier run is not this run's: an init (or a Codex turn start) after the last result means the
    # run that just exited produced none (a resumed run that died, or was stopped, before its first answer)
    r = {} if info["running_after_result"] else (info["result"] or {})
    runs = meta.get("runs") or []
    since = hc.dt.datetime.fromisoformat(runs[-1]["at"]) if runs else hc.now() - hc.dt.timedelta(days=1)
    clean = a.code == 0 and r and not r.get("is_error") and r.get("subtype") == "success"
    if clean and status_seen(stage, meta["tag"], since):
        return 0
    try:
        if not claim_exit(stage, meta):  # an observer already reported this run's end
            return 0
    except OSError:
        pass  # an unwritable state dir must not cost the EXIT line
    if clean:
        word, why = ("REVIEWED" if is_review_role(meta) else "ENDED"), "finished, no status word in the journal"
    else:
        word, why = "EXIT", (f"{r.get('subtype')}, error" if r.get("is_error") else
                             (r.get("subtype") or "no result — died or killed"))
    last = (info["last_text"] or "").strip().splitlines()
    print(hc.journal_append(stage, meta["tag"], f"{word} {a.role}: {why}; code {a.code}, turns {turns_text(info)}"
                            f"{'; last: ' + last[-1][:160] if last else ''} — agent status {a.role}"))
    return 0


def parse_send(argv: list) -> argparse.Namespace:
    """`agent send [--stage S] [--resume-anyway] R text… [--resume-anyway]`: the options may stand anywhere before a `--`;
    the first other word is the role and everything after it is the message, a word that starts with `-` included
    (argparse would take it for an option, and older versions stop the text at an option). After `--` every word is
    the role or the text."""
    stage, resume_anyway, words, rest = None, False, [], list(argv[1:])
    while rest:
        w = rest.pop(0)
        if w == "--":
            words += rest
            break
        if w == "--resume-anyway":
            resume_anyway = True
        elif w == "--stage" or w.startswith("--stage="):
            if w == "--stage":
                if not rest:
                    raise hc.UsageError("--stage needs a value")
                w = "--stage=" + rest.pop(0)
            stage = w.split("=", 1)[1]
            if stage.startswith("-"):
                raise hc.UsageError(f"--stage needs a stage name, got {stage!r}")
        elif w.startswith("-") and w != "-" and not words and not w.startswith("- "):
            raise hc.UsageError(f"agent send: unknown option {w!r} (a message goes after the role)")
        else:
            words.append(w)
    if not words:
        raise hc.UsageError("agent send: the role is required")
    return argparse.Namespace(cmd="send", role=words[0], text=words[1:], stage=stage, resume_anyway=resume_anyway)


def main(argv: list) -> int:
    prog = os.path.basename(sys.argv[0])
    sub_from_name = {"agent-spawn": "spawn", "agent-status": "status", "agent-send": "send", "agent-stop": "stop"}
    if prog in sub_from_name:
        argv = [sub_from_name[prog]] + argv
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="agent", description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    s = sub.add_parser("spawn", help="start a headless agent")
    s.add_argument("--stage")
    s.add_argument("--role", required=True)
    s.add_argument("--cwd", required=True)
    s.add_argument("--engine", choices=engines.ENGINES, help="AGENT_HUB_ENGINE, detected Codex host, else claude")
    s.add_argument("--sandbox", choices=engines.SANDBOXES, help="Codex sandbox; approval prompts remain disabled")
    s.add_argument("--sandbox-policy", help="Codex rollout sandbox JSON; preserve supported roots/network/temp restrictions")
    s.add_argument("--model", help="opus | sonnet | haiku | fable (passed to the CLI, which resolves them to its "
                   "latest models; $AGENT_HUB_MODEL_MAP pins them to ids instead) or a full id claude-…")
    s.add_argument("--effort", choices=tuple(dict.fromkeys(EFFORTS + engines.CODEX_EFFORTS)), help="default: $AGENT_HUB_EFFORT_DEFAULTS for the model, else $AGENT_HUB_DEFAULT_EFFORT, else high")
    s.add_argument("--permission-mode", help=f"default: $AGENT_HUB_PERMISSION_MODE or {DEFAULT_PERMISSION_MODE}")
    s.add_argument("--brief", required=True)
    s.add_argument("--mcp", metavar="inherit|none|FILE[,FILE]",
                   help="Claude: the MCP servers of the agent — inherit (the user's config, plugins and claude.ai "
                        "connectors), none, or only those of MCP config files; default: $AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_MCP, else none")
    s.add_argument("--worktree", nargs="?", const="", default=None, metavar="BRANCH",
                   help="run in a worktree of BRANCH (default agent/<role>): the existing one, else <repo>/.worktrees/<BRANCH> "
                        "on a new branch from origin's default branch (--base)")
    s.add_argument("--base", metavar="REF", help="with --worktree: start a new branch from REF (default: origin's default "
                   "branch after a fetch; --base HEAD is the checked-out commit of --cwd)")
    s.add_argument("--tag")
    s.add_argument("--title", help="default: <role> — <the brief's first heading> (<stage>)")
    s.add_argument("--reason", help="why the work needs an effort or a model above the default "
                   "(AGENT_HUB_EFFORT_DEFAULTS, AGENT_HUB_REASON_MODELS), or why it runs over the limit-pace stop; "
                   "journaled and kept in meta.json")
    s.add_argument("--task-class", choices=limit_pace.CLASSES,
                   help="what the work needs: mechanical | bounded (from a finished design) | judgement; default: by "
                        "the model. The limit-pace advice uses it (effort above the class default, the equivalent "
                        "class on the other engine)")
    s.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true",
                   help="run every check and print the limit-pace advice, then stop: nothing is started or written")
    s.add_argument("--ignore-hold", action="store_true",
                   help="spawn although the watchdog holds spawns for machine load (AGENT_HUB_SPAWN_HOLD_LOAD)")
    st = sub.add_parser("status", help="alive or not, model, last event age, turns")
    st.add_argument("role", nargs="?")
    st.add_argument("--stage")
    st.add_argument("--all", action="store_true")
    se = sub.add_parser("send", help="message an agent (alive → inbox, gone → resume)")
    se.add_argument("role")
    se.add_argument("text", nargs="*", help="text; without text, resume with the unread inbox messages")
    se.add_argument("--stage")
    se.add_argument("--resume-anyway", action="store_true",
                    help="resume a stopped agent although its context is above AGENT_HUB_RESUME_MAX_CTX")
    sp = sub.add_parser("stop", help="stop the agent and retire its role")
    sp.add_argument("role")
    sp.add_argument("--stage")
    wt = sub.add_parser("worktrees", help="list the repository's worktrees; --prune removes the finished ones")
    wt.add_argument("--repo", metavar="PATH", help="a path inside the repository (default: the working directory's)")
    wt.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="the same ledger as JSON")
    wt.add_argument("--fetch", action="store_true", help="git fetch origin first (--prune does it by itself): the remote refs are otherwise as last fetched")
    wt.add_argument("--no-gh", action="store_true", help="do not ask GitHub (gh) whether a branch's pull request was merged")
    wt.add_argument("--prune", action="store_true",
                    help="remove the worktrees that are merged, clean, fully pushed and not in use; nothing else")
    wt.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true", help="with --prune: say what would be removed, remove nothing")
    wt.add_argument("--no-fetch", action="store_true", help="with --prune: do not run `git fetch origin` first")
    wt.add_argument("--delete-branches", action="store_true",
                    help="with --prune: also delete the branch of a squash-merged worktree (git branch -D; its merged pull "
                         "request holds every commit); a branch merged by ancestry always goes (git branch -d)")
    wt.add_argument("--idle-for", metavar="DUR", default=worktrees.DEFAULT_IDLE,
                    help=f"a worktree whose use is unknown counts as free after this long without a change (default {worktrees.DEFAULT_IDLE})")
    en = sub.add_parser("exit-note", help="(internal) journal an EXIT line after the agent process exits")
    en.add_argument("role")
    en.add_argument("--stage")
    en.add_argument("--code", type=int, default=0)
    a = parse_send(argv) if argv[:1] == ["send"] and not {"-h", "--help"} & set(argv[:argv.index("--")] if "--" in argv else argv) \
        else p.parse_args(argv)
    return {"spawn": cmd_spawn, "status": cmd_status, "send": cmd_send, "stop": cmd_stop,
            "worktrees": cmd_worktrees, "exit-note": cmd_exit_note}[a.cmd](a)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(hc.run_main(main, sys.argv[1:]))
